r-β (TGF-β), and contribute to immunoregulation"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":16,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":17,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:32454942"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"annotator","v":["miannu"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/32454942\">pubmed:32454942</a> Next to their interaction with adaptive immune cells, activated microglia can secrete cytotoxic cytokines and oxidative products, such as ROS and NO radicals in MS lesions thereby promoting oxidative stress and contributing to myelin destruction"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":17,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":18,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:24669294"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"annotator","v":["apalma"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/24669294\">pubmed:24669294</a> While investigating the factors that regulate macrophage arginine metabolism, Mills and colleagues found that macrophages activated in mouse strains with Th1 and Th2 backgrounds differed qualitatively in their ability to respond to the classic stimuli IFN-γ or lipopolysaccharide (LPS) or both and defined an important metabolic difference in the pathway: M1 macrophages made the toxic nitric oxide (NO), whereas M2 macrophages made the trophic polyamines"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":18,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":19,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:20219869"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"tissue_data","v":["BTO:0001103"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"annotator","v":["apalma"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/20219869\">pubmed:20219869</a> Similarly, exposure of cells to oxidative stress, in particular, nitric oxide (NO) or peroxynitrite (ONOO), can activate NF-kB and cause its translocation."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":19,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":20,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:32454942"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"annotator","v":["miannu"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/32454942\">pubmed:32454942</a> Next to their interaction with adaptive immune cells, activated microglia can secrete cytotoxic cytokines and oxidative products, such as ROS and NO radicals in MS lesions thereby promoting oxidative stress and contributing to myelin destruction"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":20,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":21,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:9346241"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":21,"n":"mechanism","v":["ph