tudies have revealed that upon TGF-beta binding several serine and threonine residues in the GS domain of TGF-beta type I receptor (T beta R-I) are phosphorylated by TGF-beta type II receptor (T beta R-II) and that the phosphorylation of GS domain is essential for TGF-beta signalingThese observations indicate that serine 172 and threonine 176 of T beta R-I are dispensable for extracellular matrix protein production but essential to the growth inhibition by TGF-beta"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":33,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:32454942"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0002417"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"annotator","v":["miannu"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/32454942\">pubmed:32454942</a> IL-1β, an inflammatory cytokine primarily expressed in activated macrophages, monocytes, and microglia, significantly contributes to MS development. IL-1β promotes differentiation of T cells into Th17 cells via the STAT3 pathway and thereby promotes and aggravates the inflammatory environment in the CNS"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":33,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":34,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:32283152"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"annotator","v":["miannu"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po